      "category": "Text",
      "text": "XXV. Upon written authorization of any employee organization participating in the payroll check-off of employee organization dues, the Employee Organization Check-off Committee shall adjust the amount to be paid to the affected organization by an amount equal to that organization's cost allocation as a member of the Municipal Labor Committee, pursuant to section 1174 subd. a, of the New York City Charter and Article 7 of the Rules of the Municipal Labor Committee, adopted October 13, 1967, or as duly amended thereafter, and pay such amount directly to the Municipal Labor Committee.",
